WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.520
Second question today, Hey David, wouldn't
free college and healthcare drastically, kneecap

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.590
military enlistment since lots of people join
the military to get those things.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:11.140
So there's two parts here.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:12.980
Question one is whether that would happen.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.010
Question two is whether it's a bad thing.

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:16.400
It is true.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:21.660
There are lots of people who go into the military
in the United States because they can't afford

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:27.760
to go to college or they are not cut out for
college and the military is one of the most

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:32.820
direct paths to earning a steady paycheck
from a reliable employer.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.130
There are other financial reasons and certainly
healthcare is another thing that the military

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:38.160
provides.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.880
There are also arguments which say that if
you improve education and healthcare and access

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:47.800
to them, you would end up with more people
enlisting because they know they can always

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:53.260
go back to getting an education and they might
feel less pressured to do it right away because

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:57.480
they know that it's always there waiting for
them in some sound sense, but I believe that

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.520
that is effectively not the right way to approach
the question.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:01.520
Number one.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:06.850
Fortunately for us, we have more than enough
people in our military and a significantly

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:10.930
bigger than necessary military force, so the
military not having enough recruits because

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:14.829
people can go to college or have healthcare
is not a realistic concern.

00:01:14.829 --> 00:01:16.990
Number two, let's go even further though.

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:20.189
People who join the military for economic
necessity.

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:25.270
I don't believe are the people that I would
prefer be in the military if we don't have

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:26.810
a draft, which we don't.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:31.539
I want the people in the military to be people
who want to be in the military, not people

00:01:31.539 --> 00:01:36.270
who have no interest in it but have no money
for education or healthcare and they join

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.270
out of desperation.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:40.060
I don't think that that's good for the military.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:44.859
This is why the recruiting that the military
does in poor areas, going to high schools

00:01:44.859 --> 00:01:50.569
where the appeal is simply economic is so
predatory and I will even go further than

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:51.569
that.

00:01:51.569 --> 00:01:56.520
If we had universal healthcare, you might
break the bottleneck that is the overloaded

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:02.039
VA hospital and improve treatment for veterans
by clearing out the VA facilities a little

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:05.809
bit by allowing people to go elsewhere.

00:02:05.809 --> 00:02:12.439
Education can make it so that when veterans
come back from serving, they have more options

00:02:12.439 --> 00:02:18.989
for jobs when they come back and they will
be a better integrated into society as opposed

00:02:18.989 --> 00:02:22.409
to often ending up concentrated in certain
fields.

00:02:22.409 --> 00:02:27.709
One other thing, tons of young people aren't
even eligible to enlist because of health

00:02:27.709 --> 00:02:33.129
issues, including obesity, which is an epidemic
in the United States.

00:02:33.129 --> 00:02:36.849
Better educated people are less likely to
be obese.

00:02:36.849 --> 00:02:41.709
Overall healthier people with access to healthcare
are less likely to be obese.

00:02:41.709 --> 00:02:48.500
It is an interesting proposition that by providing
education and healthcare to people, you will

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:54.959
reduce obesity and increase the number of
people that are medically eligible to join

00:02:54.959 --> 00:02:59.799
the military and actually grow the number
of people that are enlisting.

00:02:59.799 --> 00:03:01.010
It's something to think about.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:05.390
So I think that whenever we, we see something
like, Oh, hold on.

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:10.870
Uh, if people no longer need to join the military
because they be for healthcare or economic

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.730
reasons, the military will be hurt.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:15.500
Well, let's first figure out whether that's
true.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:20.660
And secondly, let's figure out whether it's
actually hurt if different people or fewer

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:21.720
people are enlisting.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.069
I think in this case the answer seems to be
the exact opposite.

